# Stakeholder map — {{CLIENT_NAME}}

The **five roles** every engagement needs. An unnamed role is an open question, not a blank cell.

<!-- table:stakeholder-map.five-roles role=labels key=Role  answer=Name -->

| Role | Name | What they give you | Engaged? | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Executive sponsor | {{SPONSOR}} | Budget, mandate, the definition of success that will actually be judged | | Confirm they control the budget — often they don't |
| Process owner | | The official workflow and the authority to change it | | If nobody owns it end to end, that is your first finding |
| The operator | | The real workflow, including everything undocumented | | Ask the process owner who does the work daily. Then go sit with them |
| **The exception holder** | | The routing rules that exist in exactly one person's head | | "When it's ambiguous, who decides?" **The most valuable name you'll get** |
| The systems gatekeeper | | Access, data, integration reality, what is immovable | | Engage early — **access latency is the top schedule risk** |

